    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_55ddd021",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: that_moment_when_she_realizes; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a male lion mounting a female lion, with text overlay that reads 'that moment when she realizes those guarana's & tequila weren't free.' The visual metaphor maps the female lion's apparent resignation or acceptance of the male's dominance onto a human female who has been tricked into paying for something she thought was free. The meme uses the animal imagery to imply that the female is being taken advantage of, and the humor derives from the idea that she is now 'paying the price' for her mistake. This is a misogynistic trope that objectifies women by portraying them as passive, easily deceived, and ultimately responsible for their own 'misfortunes' through their choices, even when those choices are framed as innocent or naive. The meme reinforces harmful stereotypes about women's emotional instability and susceptibility to manipulation, fitting within the 'Mysogynous' category as it contains hate against women by implying their perceived weakness and lack of agency.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_52c7c340"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
